---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Work"
  description="How Visio Nova Mundi uses the Tree of Life framework to develop community initiatives, test bounded pilots and build evidence for what may come next."
>
  <div class="work-page">
    <section class="work-hero" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Visio Nova Mundi · Tree of Life framework</p>
      <h1 id="work-title">Our work grows from one framework</h1>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p>The Tree of Life is Visio Nova Mundi’s overarching social-impact framework. It connects projects, research and practical pilots around a shared objective: finding better ways for communities, public services and institutions to work together.</p>
        <p>Its branches can explore challenges across areas such as education, health, culture, tourism, justice, transport, agriculture, employment, trade, finance, community development and other public-service systems.</p>
        <p>Visio Nova Mundi does not claim to replace governments or existing institutions. Our role is to identify problems, develop practical concepts, test them on a controlled scale, measure what happens and work with appropriate partners where the evidence supports further development.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="work-button" href="/commissioners-partners/">For Commissioners &amp; Partners <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="work-section process-section" aria-labelledby="process-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">A staged approach</p>
        <h2 id="process-title">How the Tree of Life works</h2>
        <p>Ideas move forward in stages. Each step gives us a reason to continue, refine the work or stop.</p>
        <p class="process-intent">The Tree of Life is intended to develop, test and connect ideas that could contribute to better public services, community systems and institutional collaboration across sectors and countries.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="process-list" aria-label="The process from identifying a need to building evidence">
        <li><span class="step-number">01</span><span>Identify a need</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">02</span><span>Design an intervention</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">03</span><span>Run a bounded pilot</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">04</span><span>Measure impact</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">05</span><span>Learn</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">06</span><span>Improve</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">07</span><span>Test again</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-number">08</span><span>Build evidence for larger implementation</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="work-section centre-section" aria-labelledby="centre-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Community &amp; Social Cohesion · a major branch</p>
        <h2 id="centre-title">Unity House Centre — strengthening communities under one roof</h2>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <p>The Unity House Centre (UHC) is a major community branch of the Tree of Life. Its long-term concept is to create welcoming local spaces where different communities can meet, learn from one another and work together on practical local challenges.</p>
          <p>One of its central themes is waste and resource reintegration: exploring how suitable materials and surplus resources can be redirected into useful community outcomes rather than simply being discarded.</p>
          <p>The wider model can also explore food, skills, education, cultural exchange, volunteering, community interaction and other services — but each component is tested separately before becoming part of a larger operating model.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hierarchy" role="group" aria-label="Tree of Life framework and Unity House Centre development path">
        <div class="tree-root">Tree of Life</div>
        <div class="hierarchy-columns">
          <div class="main-branch">
            <p class="branch-title">Community &amp; Social Cohesion</p>
            <span class="down-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
            <p class="centre-node">Unity House Centre</p>
            <ol class="evidence-path" aria-label="Potential evidence path for the Unity House Centre">
              <li>Pilot 1</li>
              <li>Pilot 2</li>
              <li>Pilot 3</li>
              <li>Evidence</li>
              <li>Validated Centre Model</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="diagram-note">A validated model is a possible future outcome, not an assumption about current impact.</p>
          </div>
          <aside class="parallel-branches">
            <h3>Other branches can grow alongside</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Education</li>
              <li>Rural development</li>
              <li>Culture</li>
              <li>Technology</li>
              <li>Public-service innovation</li>
            </ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="work-section testing-section" aria-labelledby="testing-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current activity · bounded pilot</p>
        <h2 id="testing-title">Testing community impact before building the wider model</h2>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <p>The current six-session pilot is an early Unity House Centre discovery programme. It is not the completed Centre. Its purpose is to test assumptions about participation, community interaction, practical activities and potential social impact.</p>
          <p>We will use participant feedback, observations and partner input to understand what works, what does not, what safeguards are required and which ideas are worth testing next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="evidence-callout">One pilot will not prove the Unity House Centre model.</p>
      <p class="testing-next">The intention is to run a sequence of progressively better-defined pilots. Each pilot should answer a specific question and contribute evidence to the overall model. The Unity House Centre should only grow when the evidence, partnerships, safeguarding and financial model support doing so.</p>

      <dl class="stage-definitions" aria-label="Current, proposed and long-term Unity House Centre stages">
        <div>
          <dt><span class="stage-dot current" aria-hidden="true"></span>Testing now</dt>
          <dd>The awarded scope is six hosted community health and wellbeing sessions for adults in South Waltham Forest during September 2026–March 2027. The pilot is still within its delivery window; this does not mean all sessions have taken place.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><span class="stage-dot proposed" aria-hidden="true"></span>Proposed</dt>
          <dd>Further community activities would be designed as separate pilots, with a clear question, suitable partners and agreed safeguards.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt><span class="stage-dot vision" aria-hidden="true"></span>Long-term vision</dt>
          <dd>A permanent Unity House Centre model could be considered only if evidence, partnerships, safeguarding and a viable financial model support it.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <a class="text-link" href="/unity-house/">Read the current pilot scope <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="work-section connection-section" aria-labelledby="connection-title">
      <div class="future-label"><span class="stage-dot proposed" aria-hidden="true"></span>Future / proposed pilot</div>
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2 id="connection-title">Bringing people together safely</h2>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <p>A future pilot could examine whether structured community activities can help reduce isolation and build stronger relationships between people from different backgrounds and generations.</p>
          <p>Subject to consent, safeguarding, appropriate insurance, venue arrangements and partner approval, activities could include hosted cultural gatherings, intergenerational sessions, park walks, cooking activities and companionship programmes for older people experiencing isolation.</p>
          <p>Activities involving private homes or vulnerable participants would not take place without appropriate risk assessment, safeguarding procedures and clear participant protections.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="work-section roadmap-section" aria-labelledby="roadmap-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Learning before expansion</p>
        <h2 id="roadmap-title">A pilot roadmap shaped by evidence</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="roadmap">
        <li>
          <p class="roadmap-status"><span class="stage-dot current" aria-hidden="true"></span>Testing now</p>
          <h3><span>01</span> Community interaction</h3>
          <p>The current six-session pilot explores hosted community health, wellbeing and practical activities.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="roadmap-status"><span class="stage-dot proposed" aria-hidden="true"></span>Proposed</p>
          <h3><span>02</span> Safe social connection</h3>
          <p>A future pilot could test structured activities to support connection, subject to safeguards and partner approval.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="roadmap-status"><span class="stage-dot development" aria-hidden="true"></span>Development</p>
          <h3><span>03</span> Resource and waste reintegration</h3>
          <p>Explore suitable resource pathways with competent partners. No public collection or treatment service is established by the current pilot.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="roadmap-status"><span class="stage-dot vision" aria-hidden="true"></span>Evidence-led</p>
          <h3>Future pilots</h3>
          <p>Choose later questions in response to evidence, local need, feasibility and safeguards.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="roadmap-note">We expect the Unity House Centre concept to evolve through multiple pilots rather than being designed entirely in advance. Each stage gives us more evidence about community need, operational feasibility, cost, safeguarding and measurable impact.</p>
    </section>

    <nav class="work-links" aria-label="Related work and information">
      <a href="/projects/">Projects <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href="/governance/">Governance <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href="/contact/">Contact Visio Nova Mundi <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <style>
    .work-page {
      --work-line: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.13);
      --work-soft: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.62);
      padding-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .work-hero {
      max-width: 850px;
      padding: 12px 0 35px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 11px;
      color: #0f766e;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .09em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h1, h2, h3 { color: var(--text); }

    .work-hero h1 {
      max-width: 15ch;
      margin: 0 0 22px;
      font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 64px);
      line-height: 1.04;
      letter-spacing: -.045em;
    }

    .hero-copy, .section-copy { max-width: 82ch; }
    .hero-copy p, .section-copy p {
      margin: 0 0 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }
    .hero-copy p:last-child, .section-copy p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .work-button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 22px;
      padding: 11px 15px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(37, 99, 235, .24);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(37, 99, 235, .09), rgba(16, 185, 129, .09));
      color: var(--text);
      font-weight: 750;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: border-color .18s ease, transform .18s ease;
    }
    .work-button:hover { border-color: rgba(37, 99, 235, .5); transform: translateY(-1px); }

    .work-section {
      margin-top: 34px;
      padding-top: 30px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--work-line);
    }

    .section-heading { max-width: 900px; }
    .section-heading h2 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: clamp(27px, 3.4vw, 36px);
      line-height: 1.16;
      letter-spacing: -.03em;
    }
    .section-heading > p:not(.eyebrow) {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }
    .process-section .process-intent { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 14px; }

    .process-list {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0 22px;
      margin: 24px 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
      counter-reset: none;
    }
    .process-list li {
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 12px;
      min-width: 0;
      min-height: 72px;
      padding: 14px 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--work-line);
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 15px;
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    .step-number {
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      flex: 0 0 30px;
      width: 30px;
      height: 30px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: rgba(15, 118, 110, .1);
      color: #0f766e;
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 850;
    }

    .centre-section { padding-bottom: 2px; }
    .hierarchy {
      margin-top: 24px;
      padding: 19px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(37, 99, 235, .16);
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(37, 99, 235, .045), rgba(16, 185, 129, .055));
    }
    .tree-root, .centre-node {
      width: fit-content;
      max-width: 100%;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 10px 16px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .2);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .82);
      color: var(--text);
      font-weight: 800;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .tree-root { background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(37, 99, 235, .11), rgba(16, 185, 129, .1)); }
    .hierarchy-columns {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.7fr) minmax(220px, .8fr);
      gap: 24px;
      margin-top: 20px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--work-line);
    }
    .main-branch { min-width: 0; text-align: center; }
    .branch-title {
      margin: 0;
      color: #0f766e;
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: .03em;
    }
    .down-arrow { display: block; margin: 7px 0; color: #0f766e; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1; }
    .centre-node { border-radius: 13px; }
    .evidence-path {
      display: flex;
      align-items: stretch;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 0;
      margin: 17px 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }
    .evidence-path li {
      position: relative;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      flex: 1 1 0;
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 10px 13px;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .56);
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 750;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }
    .evidence-path li:first-child { border-left: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27); border-radius: 12px 0 0 12px; }
    .evidence-path li:last-child { border-right: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27); border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0; background: rgba(16, 185, 129, .09); }
    .evidence-path li + li::before { content: "→"; position: absolute; z-index: 1; left: -7px; top: 50%; color: #0f766e; transform: translateY(-50%); }
    .diagram-note { margin: 10px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.55; }
    .parallel-branches {
      align-self: center;
      padding: 4px 0 4px 21px;
      border-left: 1px solid var(--work-line);
    }
    .parallel-branches h3 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.4; }
    .parallel-branches ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
    .parallel-branches li { padding: 6px 9px; border: 1px solid var(--work-line); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--work-soft); color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }

    .testing-section { border-top-color: rgba(15, 118, 110, .23); }
    .evidence-callout {
      margin: 21px 0 12px;
      padding: 15px 18px;
      border-left: 4px solid #0f766e;
      border-radius: 0 13px 13px 0;
      background: linear-gradient(100deg, rgba(16, 185, 129, .11), rgba(37, 99, 235, .05));
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 19px;
      font-weight: 800;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    .testing-next { max-width: 88ch; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.75; }
    .stage-definitions {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0 22px;
      margin: 22px 0 0;
      padding: 17px 0 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--work-line);
    }
    .stage-definitions div { min-width: 0; }
    .stage-definitions dt, .future-label, .roadmap-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 8px;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 800;
    }
    .stage-definitions dd { margin: 7px 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }
    .stage-dot { display: inline-block; flex: 0 0 9px; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: #0f766e; }
    .stage-dot.proposed { background: #d97706; }
    .stage-dot.development { background: #2563eb; }
    .stage-dot.vision { background: #64748b; }
    .text-link { display: inline-flex; gap: 7px; margin-top: 17px; color: #1d4ed8; font-weight: 750; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

    .connection-section {
      padding: 20px 22px 22px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(217, 119, 6, .18);
      border-radius: 18px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .45);
    }
    .future-label { width: fit-content; margin-bottom: 13px; color: #854d0e; }
    .connection-section .section-heading h2 { margin-bottom: 10px; }

    .roadmap {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 0 18px;
      margin: 20px 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }
    .roadmap li { min-width: 0; padding: 16px 0 4px; border-top: 1px solid var(--work-line); }
    .roadmap-status { margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .045em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .roadmap h3 { margin: 0 0 7px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
    .roadmap h3 span { color: #0f766e; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .roadmap li > p:last-child { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; }
    .roadmap-note { margin: 21px 0 0; padding: 15px 17px; border: 1px solid var(--work-line); border-radius: 14px; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .58); color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }

    .work-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px 24px;
      margin-top: 30px;
      padding-top: 19px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--work-line);
    }
    .work-links a { color: #1d4ed8; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 750; text-decoration: none; }
    .work-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

    @media (max-width: 850px) {
      .process-list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
      .hierarchy-columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .parallel-branches { padding: 17px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--work-line); border-left: 0; }
      .roadmap { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    }
    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .work-hero { padding-top: 3px; padding-bottom: 25px; }
      .work-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(38px, 11vw, 50px); }
      .hero-copy p, .section-copy p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.72; }
      .work-section { margin-top: 26px; padding-top: 23px; }
      .process-list, .stage-definitions, .roadmap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .process-list { margin-top: 17px; }
      .process-list li { min-height: 0; padding: 11px 0; }
      .hierarchy { padding: 15px 12px; }
      .hierarchy-columns { gap: 19px; margin-top: 16px; padding-top: 16px; }
      .evidence-path { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: 0; margin: 14px 5px 0; }
      .evidence-path li { justify-content: flex-start; min-height: 40px; padding: 8px 12px; border: 0; border-left: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27); border-right: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27); border-radius: 0; }
      .evidence-path li:first-child { border-left: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27); border-radius: 12px 12px 0 0; }
      .evidence-path li:last-child { border-right: 1px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, .27); border-radius: 0 0 12px 12px; }
      .evidence-path li + li::before { content: "↓"; left: 50%; top: -10px; transform: translateX(-50%); }
      .stage-definitions { gap: 16px; margin-top: 18px; }
      .connection-section { padding: 17px 15px; }
      .roadmap { gap: 15px; }
      .roadmap li { padding-top: 12px; }
      .work-links { flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .work-button { transition: none; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
